  "name": "ADENOVIRUS - IgM ANTIBODY",
  "code": "2601",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>]The <strong data-start=\"59\" data-end=\"91\">Adenovirus IgM antibody test</strong> is used to detect <strong data-start=\"110\" data-end=\"139\">recent or acute infection</strong> with <strong data-start=\"145\" data-end=\"159\">adenovirus</strong>, a group of viruses that can cause respiratory illness, gastroenteritis, conjunctivitis, and other systemic infections.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Test Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive (Reactive) IgM</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates a <strong>recent or current adenovirus infection</strong>. IgM antibodies usually appear within <strong>1 week</strong> of infection and may persist for several weeks.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Negative (Non-Reactive) IgM</strong></td>\n<td>No recent adenovirus infection or the test was performed too early (before IgM response developed). Consider repeat testing if clinical suspicion is high.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Equivocal</strong></td>\n<td>Borderline result; may require <strong>repeat testing</strong> or further investigation.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
